a day after leaving taipei u.s house  speaker nancy pelosi met the speaker of  south korea's national assembly in seoul  she appeared unbothered by the  controversy sparked by her visit to  taiwan  and spoke warmly of the military and  economic relationship between south  korea and the united states  a relationship that began  from urgency  and security many years ago has become  the warmest of friendships but pelosi  left troubled waters in her wake  chinese military helicopters fly over  the taiwan strait of pingtan in southern  china at the start of live fire  exercises that effectively surround the  island  chinese state tv broadcast video of  missiles fired from the mainland into  target areas close to territorial waters  taiwan claims as its own with its  fighter jets in the air in combined  exercises designed to show china is in  complete control  the purpose is to show that the people's  liberation army is capable of  controlling the taiwan island a great  deterrent to taiwan's independent  secessionist forces nonetheless china's  foreign ministry blamed escalating  tensions firmly on the united states  if these countries really cared about  peace and stability in the taiwan strait  they should have persuaded the united  states not to engage in dangerous  reckless and irresponsible provocations  against china before pelosi's visit to  taiwan they pretended to be deaf and  silent but now they jumped out to  criticize china's just actions exposing  their hypocrisy and ugliness  china's live fire exercises are expected  to continue for the next few days  possibly even until early next week  by that time nancy pelosi will be back  in the united states but the impact of  her visit to taiwan will be felt here  for some time to come tony chang al  jazeera  taiwan's defense ministry says it's used  flares to drive away drones flying over  one of its islands close to mainland  china the incident happened in the  straits between taiwan and china there  are a number of taiwanese islands closer  to the mainland than taiwan let's take a  look kinman is the set of islands  overflown by the drones in the 1950s it  was shelled by china the u.s considered  using nuclear weapons to protect it xiyu  is part of the kinman islands that's the  chinese mainland in the back of the  photo there  china's warned ships to avoid the area  for 72 hours because of ports like xi'an  men half the world's annual shipping  goes through this area  earlier i spoke to wen t song who is a  specialist in china taiwan relations  with the australian national  university's taiwan studies program he  believes beijing's military drills are  an attempt to de-legitimize  taipei's claim of autonomy  that part of the world near taiwan  straight accounts for more or less half  the world's maritime commerce so in that  sense it's certainly a very critical  ceiling of communication uh choke point  in a way  which is also why it's raising a lot of  interest as was concerned for other  countries in the region  at this point though i think  the fact that china designates its areas  for military drill in this particular  way  may potentially be a sign of  reassurance however ironic it may sound  because  for me the way i read it is that china  is doing the ministry drill in those six  areas three of which overlap with part  of taiwan's territorial waters  precisely because china is more about  diplomatic messaging more so than  preparing for next round of major  military offenses  and the way to think about it is that  they are trying to counter the  diplomatic message of nancy pelosi's  trip to taiwan the logic is pelosi being  such a senior official building taiwan  somehow  helped legitimizes and strengthens  thailand claim  to be a sovereign state actor  and so china now is trying to counter  that effect by showing no taiwan is not  a sovereign state actor i'm gonna show  you by saying  i'm gonna do military drills in taiwan's  territorial waters i'm gonna ban  maritime shipping  during or throughout thailand's  territorial waters as well just to show  that taiwan does not have true autonomy  to govern those places and therefore  it's going to delete the mice and weaken  taiwan's claim to its own  autonomy and self-governance
 

